{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And He formed from the soil.</b> This formation is the making spoken of above — ״וַיַּעַשׂ אֱלֹהִים אֶת חַיַּת הָאָרֶץ״ and so forth — only it comes and specifies that the birds were created from the mud, since above it said they were created from the waters and here it says they were created from the earth (Hullin 27). And further, it teaches you here that at the time of their formation, immediately, on that very day, He brought them to the man to name. And in aggadic terms, this יְצִירָה is a term of subjugation and conquest, as in ״כִּי תָצוּר אֶל עִיר״ (Deuteronomy 24) — that He subdued them under the hand of man (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And whatsoever the man would call every living creature, etc.</b> Invert it and expound it: every living creature that the man would name — that is its name forever."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:20.486181896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}